            <fr:meta name="toc">true</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <fr:p>Incorrect software specifications are a problem because
    they can invalidate the security guarantees offered by <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-000X.xml" addr="dhsorens-000X" title="Formal Specification and Verification">formal verification</fr:link>, 
    offer a false sense of security,
    misguide developers,
    and most importantly open code up to vulnerabilities.
    Indeed, for <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-000Y.xml" addr="dhsorens-000Y" title="Smart Contracts">smart contracts</fr:link>, poor specifications are a <fr:link type="local" href="dhsorens-001P.xml" addr="dhsorens-001P" title="Smart Contract Vulnerabilities Due to Poor Specification">common source of catastrophic vulnerabilities and losses of funds</fr:link>.</fr:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
